From: DKR-R Win95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Open streams from path.string(), never from the path

On MinGW, std::filesystem::path::value_type is wchar_t. Passing a path to a
stream constructor therefore opens the file through _wfopen -- the wide CRT --
and Windows 95 exports that whole family as stubs: the binary loads, and every
open silently fails.

The failure is not obvious from the code. It surfaced as a save test dying on
"Could not create the temporary save file" while the same code passed on the
host, and the import table was no help: _wfopen is present, because a stub is
present. Measured on the machine with tools/win95/witnesses/wide_stream_probe.cpp:

    ofstream(path)             FAILS
    ofstream(path.string())    works
    ifstream(path)             FAILS
    ifstream(path.string())    works

path.string() is narrow on every platform and yields the same bytes elsewhere,
so this costs nothing on the targets that already worked. It is applied to the
five sites librecomp uses outside its mod system.

---

--- a/librecomp/src/files.cpp
+++ b/librecomp/src/files.cpp
@@ -4,14 +4,29 @@
 constexpr std::u8string_view backup_suffix = u8".bak";
 constexpr std::u8string_view temp_suffix = u8".temp";
 
+// Streams are opened from path.string() and never from the path itself.
+//
+// On MinGW, std::filesystem::path::value_type is wchar_t, so passing a path to
+// a stream constructor opens the file through _wfopen -- the wide CRT. Windows
+// 95 exports that family as stubs: the binary loads and every open fails.
+//
+// Measured on the machine (tools/win95/witnesses/wide_stream_probe.cpp):
+//
+//     ofstream(path)             FAILS
+//     ofstream(path.string())    works
+//     ifstream(path)             FAILS
+//     ifstream(path.string())    works
+//
+// path.string() is narrow on every platform and identical elsewhere, so this
+// costs nothing on the targets that were already working.
 std::ifstream recomp::open_input_backup_file(const std::filesystem::path& filepath, std::ios_base::openmode mode) {
     std::filesystem::path backup_path{filepath};
     backup_path += backup_suffix;
-    return std::ifstream{backup_path, mode};
+    return std::ifstream{backup_path.string(), mode};
 }
 
